---
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/agent-config-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/agent-config-dark.svg?raw';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={400}
  caption="The repo supplies shared settings. Each tool keeps its sessions, credentials, and local choices."
>
  The private ~/.agents repo holds shared instructions, skills, and config.
  Claude Code uses links for settings and skills. Codex syncs selected settings
  and discovers skills in the shared store. opencode uses linked settings and
  discovers the same skills. Sessions, credentials, databases, and local
  approvals stay on the machine, outside shared-config sync.
</Diagram>
